    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Add a Loading State",
    "long_instructions": "# Add a Loading State\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Make it obvious that your app is working while it waits for API data.\r\n\r\n1. **Choose a Loading Indicator:** Decide what you will show, such as \"Loading...\" text, a spinner, or a simple skeleton area.\r\n2. **Show Loading Immediately:** As soon as the user clicks the button, display your loading indicator before the fetch finishes.\r\n3. **Hide Loading When Done:** After the data loads and renders, remove or hide the loading indicator.\r\n4. **Test It:** Click your button and confirm the loading state appears right away and disappears when results show.\r\n\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Show a clear \"Loading...\" message or spinner right away when the user clicks, so the app never feels frozen while it waits for data. ***(supports completing Milestone 3 tasks)***",
